From 1d7feb0d149d6aea7d697bb0bc4755cb8b37a6dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 08:57:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] qos v5.1: policer burst/rate fixes from metal tuning
 (2026-07-15)

Owner metal iteration results (router built-in WAN speedtest, no wifi hop):
- qos_ibw at ~100% of measured line + any bucket size: throughput collapse
  (reaches line rate, then synchronized multi-stream TCP backoff halves it
  repeatedly until the transfer aborts; Cloudflare read ~1/6 of line).
- qos_ibw at ~90% of measured (2150400 kbps on a 2353 Mb/s line) + 100ms
  bucket (26,880,000 bytes): holds 2071 Mb/s steady, ping DROPS 10.2->8.7ms,
  jitter 0.57ms. The feature works; the old 10ms bucket and the at-line-rate
  guidance gap were the failures.

Changes:
1. burst = ~100ms of rate (ibw*12.5 bytes), floor 64KB, cap 100MB (the
   rdpa_policer.h CBS legal max; old code capped at 8MB which silently
   truncated the needed bucket on multi-gig links).
2. stop branch: getportrxrate readback guard - skip the clear when already
   (0, 0, 0), silencing the one-time kernel ERR _drv_policer_clear_profile
   observed on the first apply after boot.
3. WMM stamp goes LIFT-ONLY: the v1.5.3 map demoted Q5 to CS1/AC_BK, but Q5
   in the shipped class template is the catch-all DEFAULT class - so nearly
   all wifi-bound traffic (including upload ACK streams) rode the starved
   background AC. Metal: healthy 6GHz/320MHz client read 433/265 Mb/s with
   1.5% loss and 77ms jitter, policer off. Now only Q1->CS6 and Q2->CS5 are
   stamped; Q3/Q4/Q5 stay at best-effort. Rule: never stamp the default
   class down.
4. RQOS_117/RQOS_119 (all 25 dicts): never-100% policer warning; lift-only
   wording.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
